  {'post_id': 9, 'day': 7, 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'content': "Been running NovaMind Assistant in production for ~2 months. Performance is solid—throughput and response times are competitive. Main friction point: the usage tier limits are a hard wall. Hit my monthly cap mid-sprint last week and everything just... stops. No graceful degradation, no overflow option. Had to either wait 30 days or upgrade mid-cycle, which throws off my cost modeling.\n\nThe platform itself delivers what it promises—reliable, good token efficiency. But the pricing model feels optimized for predictability rather than flexibility. Works fine if your workload is flat and you've got perfect forecasting. Not so much for variable demand. Decent value if you nail your tier estimate; otherwise you're either bleeding money or hitting walls.\n\nWould be worth reconsidering if they offered burst capacity or usage-based overage at reasonable rates. Right now it's a trade-off between cost certainty and operational friction."}
